{"diagnosis": "Fetch test reports `TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000` with `tohost: FAIL 0xdead` instead of advancing through 256-word NOP mem. Expected max_addr to progress beyond 0x00000000 as fetches complete. Root cause in excerpt at picorv32.v:1408 where `set_mem_do_wdata = 1` forces write-phase every cycle and blocks `launch_next_insn` fetch progress at picorv32.v:1400, so PC never advances.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1402,7 +1402,7 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
 		trap <= 0;
 		reg_sh <= 'bx;
 		reg_out <= 'bx;
 		set_mem_do_rinst = 0;
 		set_mem_do_rdata = 0;
-		set_mem_do_wdata = 1;
+		set_mem_do_wdata = 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: no progress, max_addr advances beyond 0x00000000"}

